We agree there. I don't know what to do about it, either. Crawl's system  
is attractive, but it's not Nethack compatible[*]. Except perhaps for  
the skill system. And perhaps that alone would be enough to add some  
diversity, if some restrictions were also removed. (What's the point of  
needing a certain alignment and XL for the quest, plus the inability to  
change alignment more than once? That's where more options, for  
different paths, could be inserted, for example.)

With the skill system, you can _try_ anything, you're just no good at  
learning some things, so it takes much longer to get really good at it.  
(Which is a choice that I think should be left to the player. Insert  
time taken into the afair useless-as-is score to reflect that.)

Then there's race abilities. With that, the abilities of potentially  
added races can be varied. (To take a Crawl example; Mummies can't eat  
at all, and IIRC don't need nutrition. Not that I'm saying this is or is  
not a Nethack compatible trait, it's just an example.)

[*] The big incompatibility lies in how excitement is created; Crawl is  
ruled by the Raving Nuts God, Nethack gives you a fair chance. Both  
interesting in themselves but you can't transfer the whim of Xom to  
Nethack without losing the fair chance. (And I think it should keep  
that.)

For the excitement, more variety in the endgame would help. (Different  
types of paths down, so you don't know what to expect before you get  
there.)

